# Convex client and types

## Client (`src/`)

- Import `api` from `@/lib/convex`. Import `useQuery` / `useMutation` from `convex/react`.
- Do not `fetch("/api/...")` for domain data. Do not add a parallel REST layer.
- Skip queries when there is no session: `useQuery(api.auth.getCurrentUser, token ? { token } : "skip")`.
- Auth helpers stay in `src/context/AuthContext.tsx` and `src/hooks/useAuth.ts`. Role checks in `src/services/permissions.ts`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { useQuery, useMutation } from "convex/react";
import { api } from "@/lib/convex";

const user = useQuery(api.auth.getCurrentUser, token ? { token } : "skip");
const login = useMutation(api.auth.login);
```

## Types

- Convex document types come from generated `Id<"table">` (`@/lib/convex` re-exports `Id`).
- Shared UI unions (e.g. `UserRole`) live next to the consumer (`AuthContext`) or in `convex/lib/` validators (`userRole` in `convex/lib/roles.ts`).
- Do not invent Zod/Directus schemas. Validators belong in Convex (`v.union(v.literal(...))`).
- camelCase fields, matching `schema.ts` (`firstName`, not `first_name`).
